title: 'a-clock: stop wake-from-sleep admin-prompt nagging'
summary: 'Fixed constant osascript/admin-password prompts from the wake-from-sleep feature. Root cause: scheduling a pmset wake needs root (osascript ''with administrator privileges''), and the ''already scheduled'' dedup lived only in RAM, so every app launch re-prompted — amplified by the KeepAlive agent and frequent reinstalls, which also created duplicate wakes. Fix: persist the last-scheduled wake time to localStorage so it only prompts when the earliest alarm time actually changes (and cancels the prior before adding, preventing duplicates), default wakeFromSleep to OFF (opt-in), and bump the settings storage key to v2 so existing installs reset with wake off. Verified the app now launches adding no new wakes and no prompt.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#wake'
  - '#storage'
files_modified:
  - src/lib/wake.ts
  - src/lib/storage.ts
decisions:
  - id: persist-wake-dedup
    decision: Persist the last-scheduled wake time to localStorage
    rationale: The in-RAM dedup reset every launch, so pmset (which needs an admin prompt) re-ran on each start; persisting means it only prompts when the earliest alarm changes.
  - id: wake-opt-in
    decision: Default wake-from-sleep OFF and bump settings key to v2
    rationale: Wake-from-sleep is heavyweight (admin prompt) and shouldn't be on unless the user asks; the key bump resets existing installs that had the old default-on behavior.
learnings:
  - Any per-session dedup guarding an admin-prompting side effect must be persisted, or every process restart re-triggers the prompt — especially under a launchd KeepAlive that restarts the app.
  - pmset schedule wake without cancelling the prior creates duplicate wake events.
